NuSTAR libsais40-v1

Derived from libsais 2.12.1 by Ilya Grebnov, copyright 2021-2026.
Upstream: https://github.com/IlyaGrebnov/libsais/tree/v2.12.1
License: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception; see LICENSE.
The exact source/archive hashes are recorded in ../libsais/libsais_upstream.json.

NuSTAR changes:
- Five-byte signed array slots with native-width scalar arithmetic and fixed caches.
- Explicit logical 40-bit casts and two marker bits; input bound below 2^38-1.
- Slot-based views for scratch records, and slot-relative bucket placement.
- Workspace-preserving, alignment-aware 40/32-bit recursive conversion.
- Native SIMD kernels that assume eight-byte entries disabled in the compact path.
- Only suffix-array construction is exported; unused kernels are removed.
- Final NuSTAR packed SA reuses the original allocation (see index/packed_suffix_array.cpp).

regenerate.py deterministically derives libsais40.inc from the pinned vendored
libsais64.c. It refuses a changed upstream hash. Regeneration does not download
code. slot.hpp and native_recursion.hpp are the maintained storage adapters.

Memory scope: the main SA and reduced text share five-byte storage. As in
libsais, recursive alphabet buckets can use extra storage when workspace is
insufficient: five-byte entries in the compact recursion or four-byte entries
inside native libsais_int. This is not a claim of 5N plus O(1) total scratch.
No full-length 64-bit SA, ISA, or recursive text is allocated by this backend.
